  "result": "I fixed it. Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/core.py:392`, when a subcommand's context was created, it was given the parent's entire `default_map`. It should only get the entry under its own name. So `default_map={\"sub\": {\"name\": \"...\"}}` made the subcommand look for `name` at the top level, never found it, and silently fell back to the option's normal default.\n\n**Fix:** That line is now `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. This is the behaviour documented for Click: each subcommand gets the nested dictionary keyed by its own name.\n\n**Checked:**\n- A small script with a group and a `sub` command now prints the value from `default_map` (`fromdm`). It used to print the hard-coded default.\n- The test suite passes: 1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed. pytest also reported 31,000 tests as deselected; I didn't look into why.\n\nI didn't add a regression test for this case. I haven't committed anything.",
